{
  "_about": "The listing match vocabulary for match.js (tools/site/build_resume.py copies it into match.js). Each key is a canonical term. A term on the record lists the builds.json proof ids that verify it; off: true marks a term that is not on Jason's verified record (a gap, or something he has not confirmed), which the match names and never claims; ignore: true consumes a phrase so a shorter term inside it does not count. aliases are the spellings listings use (the key itself counts too, unless key is false, and matches case-sensitively when an =key alias is listed); hyphens and spaces are interchangeable, a trailing s is allowed unless plural is false, case: true matches every alias case-sensitively and an alias starting = matches case-sensitively, not lists regexes that cancel a match they cover, and an alias starting re: is a regex (a group 1, when present, is the span). Matching takes the longest phrase first. facts answer degree and years-of-experience requirements with text that is already in llms.txt, never with a verdict.",
